{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-125668" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/assets/6ed50407066da9fc213202ccff8c8be06c89d2dce0f5dfe07877cab77c98b3ec.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $E$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $E$ is traversed once in the **clockwise** direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ac6e16e9b1dbfaf7336b11f1754dd3b4a5e0b286fe0bd91a2cf6479cb3d5dd"} {"question" "q-125668" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. Since the force $F$ acts perpendicular to the motion of the particle as it moves around $C,$ it neither helps nor hinders its motion. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/assets/045f6867a50dff0c162376015cc4651de796d0a637643b4b5ba402ef55dde4fa.png)\n\nSo, ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ remains unchanged.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/assets/698f68b9539e6ef5c4b07dbe6cf3859449e2687db19406f6c2b0072fa5eb697e.png)\n\nSo, ${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ac6e16e9b1dbfaf7336b11f1754dd3b4a5e0b286fe0bd91a2cf6479cb3d5dd"} {"question" "q-125668" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b0739c96ad346238c47110cc19d8571d34c4c37477e99709f7d89249005e6827"} {"question" "q-125668" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ac6e16e9b1dbfaf7336b11f1754dd3b4a5e0b286fe0bd91a2cf6479cb3d5dd"} {"question" "q-125668" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ac6e16e9b1dbfaf7336b11f1754dd3b4a5e0b286fe0bd91a2cf6479cb3d5dd"} {"question" "q-125668" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ac6e16e9b1dbfaf7336b11f1754dd3b4a5e0b286fe0bd91a2cf6479cb3d5dd"} {"question" "q-125637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/assets/e60f7c0adc3e2ec8daa3203564c31bf660e6eca7e6394955cc73133ac3673ed5.png)\n\nConsider the circle $S$ and the vector field $F,$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ac6e16e9b1dbfaf7336b11f1754dd3b4a5e0b286fe0bd91a2cf6479cb3d5dd"} {"question" "q-125637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement III is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves counterclockwise along $C.$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/assets/a8010db8481768cb61d0734dcfc97eed646441ab265c4928d06d274ef0e1c1dd.png)\n\nSo, ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves **clockwise** along $C.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/assets/be263d706bfc3ef205be37aaed85d4984d3739d53cdaadb8cba88e3d5196ce93.png)\n\nSo, ${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ac6e16e9b1dbfaf7336b11f1754dd3b4a5e0b286fe0bd91a2cf6479cb3d5dd"} {"question" "q-125637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b0739c96ad346238c47110cc19d8571d34c4c37477e99709f7d89249005e6827"} {"question" "q-125637" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ac6e16e9b1dbfaf7336b11f1754dd3b4a5e0b286fe0bd91a2cf6479cb3d5dd"} {"question" "q-125637" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ac6e16e9b1dbfaf7336b11f1754dd3b4a5e0b286fe0bd91a2cf6479cb3d5dd"} {"question" "q-125637" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/referenc